WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:02.859
- [Mark] Welcome back
to the show everyone.

00:00:02.859 --> 00:00:04.650
Whether you're a kid who's
12 years old or younger

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:07.980
or an adult older than 19,
you're gonna love this episode.

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:11.790
If you're a teenager, it
may already be too late.

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:13.650
- You could give God what it takes.

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:15.740
- Mount Rushmore may have four presidents

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:18.470
but it's only got room
for three baddy slashers,

00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:21.880
Freddy Krueger, Jason
Vorhees and Michael Myers.

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:24.380
Or as I'd call them if I
wrote for the local newspaper,

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:25.880
the Enigma of Elm Street

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:28.180
versus the Killer of Camp Crystal Lake

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:30.890
versus the Haddonfield Halloween Hunk.

00:00:30.890 --> 00:00:33.890
Ah, I miss that, improv's tough, everyone.

00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:35.810
It's the debate you and
your friends have had since

00:00:35.810 --> 00:00:38.710
the dawn of time, or at least 1984.

00:00:38.710 --> 00:00:41.040
Who's the best horror movie bad guy?

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:42.540
Today, we're gonna settle just that

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:45.180
by tossing into the Vitamix
your favorite dream master,

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:47.020
the iconic undead goalie

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:49.143
and the world's meanest trick or treater.

00:00:50.163 --> 00:00:51.700
It's about to be the
most violent, goriest,

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:53.780
bloodiest threesome you've ever seen.

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:56.290
- Welcome to my nightmare.

00:00:56.290 --> 00:00:57.730
- Here's how we'll determine a winner.

00:00:57.730 --> 00:00:59.510
Round one, box office.

00:00:59.510 --> 00:01:02.560
Round two, tomato meter/audience score.

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:05.160
Round three, cultural relevance.

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:06.480
And then if I'm still alive,

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:08.960
we'll do a wild card
round to settle the score.

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:10.710
Two of these fellows
fought in a movie once

00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:11.740
and it was a good battle,

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:15.500
only problem was it
appeared to end in a draw

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:18.200
but now we're adding Michael
Myers to the VIP list

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:21.250
and only one of these three
stocking stalwarts of cinema

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:23.250
will get bragging rights in hell,

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:25.680
where I believe Jason has a summer home.

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:26.513
Let's get it on.

00:01:27.531 --> 00:01:30.190
(upbeat rock music)

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:31.110
Round one, box office.

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:34.300
The year was 1978, Jimmy
Carter was president,

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:36.170
the Pittsburgh Steelers
were etching their name

00:01:36.170 --> 00:01:37.120
into the record books

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:38.840
and parents were
concerned about their kids

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:40.890
listening to that darn Van Halen.

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:42.690
But by the time October rolled around,

00:01:42.690 --> 00:01:46.340
1978 became about one thing
this new "Halloween" movie

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:48.790
you had to see and keep your eyes open

00:01:48.790 --> 00:01:50.780
the whole time to believe.

00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:54.710
Grossing $188 million
on a shoe string budget

00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:58.157
that adjusted barely over
$1 million in today's world,

00:01:58.157 --> 00:02:00.900
"Halloween" was celebrated
as a horror film rebirth

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:03.770
and it would spawn 10 sequels/reboots

00:02:03.770 --> 00:02:07.200
that all told, have
gross 851 million bucks

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:10.210
for a $77 million per film average,

00:02:10.210 --> 00:02:11.640
those numbers are greatly enhanced

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:14.520
by the most recent entry
into the legendary franchise.

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:17.680
2018's cleverly titled "Halloween,"

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:22.500
which would total $165 million
in total domestic receipts.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:25.140
And perhaps it was the looming
presence of Michael Myers

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:27.900
that inspired Jason and Freddy
to make their own movies.

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:31.187
J-Dogs can would be up
next beginning with 1980s

00:02:31.187 --> 00:02:32.890
"Friday the 13th."

00:02:32.890 --> 00:02:33.900
- Killer mommy.

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:35.540
- Yes, I know it was Jason's mommy

00:02:35.540 --> 00:02:37.510
who was doing the stabbing
during the first one

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:39.790
but she was doing it for her boy.

00:02:39.790 --> 00:02:41.867
So even though we don't
see the iconic Jason

00:02:41.867 --> 00:02:44.700
trying out for the local
rec league hockey team look

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:46.030
until the third film,

00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:48.650
I'm giving him credit
for the entire franchise,

00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:50.220
it's what his mom would have wanted

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:52.540
and to be frank, I don't
feel like dying over it.

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:53.760
- That's a good boy.

00:02:55.060 --> 00:02:58.998
- "Friday the 13th" flicks
have racked up 862 million

00:02:58.998 --> 00:03:01.416
total bucks over the course of 12 movies

00:03:01.416 --> 00:03:05.210
making for a golf clappable
$72 million per film average.

00:03:05.210 --> 00:03:07.170
Strictly in terms of box office,

00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:09.050
the gold standard is still the original,

00:03:09.050 --> 00:03:13.474
sporting a cannon record,
$138 million resume line.

00:03:13.474 --> 00:03:16.057
(spooky music)

00:03:17.850 --> 00:03:19.230
And then there were two

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:21.030
and for most teens that would be plenty

00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:23.170
but then 1984 happened

00:03:23.170 --> 00:03:26.300
and not even your worst
Orwellian nightmare could compete

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:29.780
with the shut eye action
going down on Elm Street.

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:32.380
Freddy Krueger, a former
janitorial enthusiast

00:03:32.380 --> 00:03:34.050
with a limited wardrobe budget,

00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:36.930
debuted on the big
screen with a $68 million

00:03:36.930 --> 00:03:38.600
total domestic hall.

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:39.800
Unlike his colleagues,

00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:42.630
Fred wouldn't see his
highest solo box office

00:03:42.630 --> 00:03:45.720
until his fourth movie,
subtitled "The Dream Master,"

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:48.240
grossing 113 million bucks.

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:50.820
Kruger and his zany one-liners
have starred in a total

00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:55.820
of nine movies raking in a
combined bushel of $739 million,

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:58.781
for an average of 82 million per flick.

00:03:58.781 --> 00:03:59.731
- No pain, no gain.

00:04:01.824 --> 00:04:03.700
(woman screams)

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:05.890
- [Mark] All three fellows came
out of the box office gates

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:08.460
swinging for a very competitive round one.

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:10.760
If you look at the top
12 of their combined

00:04:10.760 --> 00:04:12.320
best moneymaking movies,

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:15.630
each psychopath has
four movies on the list,

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:18.470
but it's "Halloween"
claiming the top two spots

00:04:18.470 --> 00:04:22.180
with the 1978 and 2018 films respectively.

00:04:22.180 --> 00:04:24.940
And while "Friday the 13th"
has the highest total gross

00:04:24.940 --> 00:04:26.620
and "Nightmare on Elm Street"

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:27.487
boasts the highest per film average,

00:04:27.487 --> 00:04:30.727
"Halloween" is a close
second in both categories.

00:04:30.727 --> 00:04:32.460
And we have to point out that Mikey

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:35.367
doesn't have the advantage of
a successful crossover movie.

00:04:35.367 --> 00:04:37.640
"Freddy versus Jason" did happen

00:04:37.640 --> 00:04:41.500
and made $128 million on
its way to disappointing me

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:43.320
by not declaring a true winner.

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:45.848
- Who gives a fuck what you think?

00:04:45.848 --> 00:04:46.681
(woman screams)

00:04:46.681 --> 00:04:48.151
- [Mark] Sealing the deal for me

00:04:48.151 --> 00:04:48.984
is the return on investment.

00:04:48.984 --> 00:04:50.960
All three franchises burst onto the scene

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:54.450
with a remarkable ability
to spin straw into gold.

00:04:54.450 --> 00:04:58.360
Freddy's rookie flick cost
just $1.8 million at the time,

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:01.480
while Jason's mom's opening
budget was even lower

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:05.110
at $550,000 but it was Michael,

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:08.170
alligator arms when the
check arrives, Meyers

00:05:08.170 --> 00:05:12.810
who got his movie made for
just $325,000 at the time.

00:05:12.810 --> 00:05:14.640
And it was probably that initial success

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:16.337
that made film executives say

00:05:16.337 --> 00:05:18.140
"Hey, can we do that in a camp

00:05:18.140 --> 00:05:20.850
or over on that Boulevard
named after a tree?"

00:05:20.850 --> 00:05:24.280
- Every town has an Elm Street.

00:05:24.280 --> 00:05:26.000
- Even though he kills
people without remorse,

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:28.410
Michael makes tons of money for his crew,

00:05:28.410 --> 00:05:31.411
so he gets to win in round number one.

00:05:31.411 --> 00:05:33.090
- You can't kill the Bogeyman.

00:05:33.090 --> 00:05:36.440
- Round two, tomato meter/audience score.

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:38.310
Before I asked the usual question

00:05:38.310 --> 00:05:40.940
of sure you made money but
were the movies any good?

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:42.760
Let's go ahead and free the cats

00:05:42.760 --> 00:05:45.520
from their environmental
friendly, reusable bag.

00:05:45.520 --> 00:05:48.210
Each of these gentlemen have
made some real stinkers,

00:05:48.210 --> 00:05:50.230
you think a dismembered body smells bad?

00:05:50.230 --> 00:05:51.840
Wait until you get a whiff of how rotten

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:54.440
some of these movies
are on the tomato meter.

00:05:54.440 --> 00:05:57.140
- [Freddy] You really
shouldn't fall asleep in class.

00:05:57.140 --> 00:05:59.070
- All three guys have multiple movies

00:05:59.070 --> 00:06:01.200
that are 15% or below,

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:04.650
it's Jason taking the brunt
of it with a record low 8%

00:06:04.650 --> 00:06:06.430
for that time he took Manhattan.

00:06:06.430 --> 00:06:09.170
Taking an unwanted silver
metal is millennial of note,

00:06:09.170 --> 00:06:12.520
Paul Rudd in "Halloween:
The Curse of Michael Myers"

00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:14.498
earning just 9%.

00:06:14.498 --> 00:06:15.331
- Sorry.

00:06:15.331 --> 00:06:16.970
- And maybe the most disappointing of all

00:06:16.970 --> 00:06:19.890
would be the 2010 remake of
"Nightmare on Elm Street,"

00:06:19.890 --> 00:06:21.850
which scored 15%.

00:06:21.850 --> 00:06:23.210
That's supposed to course correct

00:06:23.210 --> 00:06:25.642
to get the franchise
back on the right path.

00:06:25.642 --> 00:06:28.380
Huh, uh, no, oh, no Robert England.

00:06:28.380 --> 00:06:31.300
Look, I love you, Jackie you
were great in "Bad News Bears"

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:34.924
but there's only one Freddy
and his name is Robbie.

00:06:34.924 --> 00:06:36.007
- It's a boy!

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:41.750
- [Mark] But so what if
they've had some missteps

00:06:41.750 --> 00:06:43.270
in their time?

00:06:43.270 --> 00:06:44.670
There's some good in there too, right?

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:46.760
Yes, in fact, there's a ton of it.

00:06:46.760 --> 00:06:49.810
The tomato meter top 10
features two movies from Jason

00:06:49.810 --> 00:06:51.160
including his only fresh flick,

00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:54.000
his mom's "Friday the 13th" at 64%

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:55.600
and three "Halloween" movies

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:57.730
headlined by the overall clubhouse leader

00:06:57.730 --> 00:07:02.730
and grand daddy of them all
1978's original with 96%.

00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:04.540
- Was it the Bogeyman?

00:07:04.540 --> 00:07:06.850
- As a matter of fact, it was.

00:07:06.850 --> 00:07:09.830
- But it's Freddy who has
five movies in the top 10,

00:07:09.830 --> 00:07:11.770
hey, that's one for each razor blade.

00:07:11.770 --> 00:07:16.080
Topping out with his original
1984 introduction at 94%.

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:18.207
And it's worth noting that while the 2010

00:07:18.207 --> 00:07:20.220
"Nightmare on Elm Street"
tanked with critics,

00:07:20.220 --> 00:07:24.400
the 1994 Metta tour de force
West Craven's new nightmare

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:26.643
is currently at 80%.

00:07:27.850 --> 00:07:28.683
- Miss me?

00:07:28.683 --> 00:07:30.180
- [Mark] But before I
give the round to Fred,

00:07:30.180 --> 00:07:32.577
let's take a gander at
that audience score.

00:07:32.577 --> 00:07:34.910
"Nightmare" and "Halloween"
each sport three movies

00:07:34.910 --> 00:07:37.389
that made it fresh with audiences,

00:07:37.389 --> 00:07:39.300
meanwhile, "Friday the
13th" only has its original

00:07:39.300 --> 00:07:42.972
bragging about being fresh barely at 60%.

00:07:42.972 --> 00:07:45.520
(woman screams)

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:47.470
And for overall audience score average,

00:07:47.470 --> 00:07:50.880
it's once again between the
dream dude and the holiday guy.

00:07:50.880 --> 00:07:55.880
Freddy's average is
50.1%, Michael's is 50.3%.

00:07:55.990 --> 00:07:58.867
You see kids, voting does matter.

00:07:58.867 --> 00:08:00.640
- Tell 'em Freddy sent ya!

00:08:00.640 --> 00:08:02.768
- And so does the tomato meter.

00:08:02.768 --> 00:08:04.320
Freddy dominates average score over there

00:08:04.320 --> 00:08:08.240
winning easily with 50.4%
over its closest competition,

00:08:08.240 --> 00:08:10.630
Michael Myers, at 37%.

00:08:10.630 --> 00:08:14.130
So, Sir Lord Krueger, round two is yours

00:08:14.130 --> 00:08:15.520
and I'm sure you'd like to celebrate

00:08:15.520 --> 00:08:19.054
with one of your classic
comedic barb's, have at it.

00:08:19.054 --> 00:08:21.040
- Now I'm playin' with power!

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:23.730
- Round three; cultural relevance.

00:08:23.730 --> 00:08:25.030
Hey, when it gets to the real reason

00:08:25.030 --> 00:08:26.270
why we're doing this vid,

00:08:26.270 --> 00:08:28.110
because people still care,

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:30.740
they love these three awful human beings

00:08:30.740 --> 00:08:32.670
and even decades after their debuts,

00:08:32.670 --> 00:08:34.980
no one in the horror game has come close

00:08:34.980 --> 00:08:37.540
to the cultural relevance
of the big three.

00:08:37.540 --> 00:08:38.980
Ghostface, good effort,

00:08:38.980 --> 00:08:41.840
Darth Maul looking guy
from 'Insidious," cool,

00:08:41.840 --> 00:08:43.320
weird dude from "Sinister,"

00:08:43.320 --> 00:08:45.533
update your home movie technology.

00:08:46.520 --> 00:08:48.050
Since Mikey came along first

00:08:48.050 --> 00:08:50.180
and decided to base his murderous rampages

00:08:50.180 --> 00:08:51.570
around a popular holiday,

00:08:51.570 --> 00:08:54.920
it's safe to say he's made it
into the hall of killer fame.

00:08:54.920 --> 00:08:57.220
It already impressive that "Halloween H20"

00:08:57.220 --> 00:08:59.090
saw a dramatic uptick in box office

00:08:59.090 --> 00:09:01.130
from previous entries in the franchise

00:09:01.130 --> 00:09:03.780
and then to do it even more
successfully 20 years later?

00:09:03.780 --> 00:09:05.870
We still crave Michael Myers.

00:09:05.870 --> 00:09:06.950
If you need more evidence,

00:09:06.950 --> 00:09:10.217
think of the iconic
slasher films before 1978,

00:09:10.217 --> 00:09:12.830
"Peeping Tom," "Black Christmas,"

00:09:12.830 --> 00:09:14.880
not exactly household names.

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:16.360
The only reason we'd mentioned "Psycho"

00:09:16.360 --> 00:09:18.520
is because of that legendary shower scene

00:09:18.520 --> 00:09:21.060
and remember who was
bleeding chocolate syrup?

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:24.330
Janet Lee, AKA Jamie Lee Curtis' mom.

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:27.650
Life is just one big NASCAR track, kids.

00:09:27.650 --> 00:09:30.610
- We've all had bad things happen to us,

00:09:30.610 --> 00:09:34.490
the trick is to concentrate on today.

00:09:34.490 --> 00:09:37.130
- [Mark] We might not have
Mr. Myers' competition today

00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:39.230
if not for his inaugural movie.

00:09:39.230 --> 00:09:42.200
And that's flick also
popularized the use of panaglide,

00:09:42.200 --> 00:09:43.810
which is how John Carpenter managed

00:09:43.810 --> 00:09:46.090
to get those super eerie
first person glimpses

00:09:46.090 --> 00:09:47.610
from Michael's perspective.

00:09:47.610 --> 00:09:49.644
Audiences were frightened,

00:09:49.644 --> 00:09:52.350
film students were like,
"Oh, it looks so smooth!"

00:09:52.350 --> 00:09:54.800
But maybe carpenter's best
contribution to the legacy

00:09:54.800 --> 00:09:58.580
of the shape is the musical
score that he composed himself.

00:09:58.580 --> 00:10:00.480
You know it instantly and it may be second

00:10:00.480 --> 00:10:03.990
only to "Jaws" as far as
themes that can instantly scare

00:10:03.990 --> 00:10:05.630
the hell out of you.

00:10:05.630 --> 00:10:07.580
Oh, do I smell a crossover?

00:10:07.580 --> 00:10:10.663
Could a shark pull off
wearing that "Halloween" mask?

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:15.400
Speaking of memorable themes,

00:10:15.400 --> 00:10:17.597
how about a little kid belting out

00:10:17.597 --> 00:10:21.083
♪ One, two, Freddy's comin' for you ♪

00:10:21.083 --> 00:10:25.550
♪ Three, four, better lock your door ♪

00:10:25.550 --> 00:10:28.270
Ominous lyrics plus singing children?

00:10:28.270 --> 00:10:30.300
That's a Coca Cola level formula

00:10:30.300 --> 00:10:32.170
that equals pure creepiness.

00:10:32.170 --> 00:10:36.780
- [Freddy] The only thing
to fear is fear himself.

00:10:36.780 --> 00:10:39.410
- Freddy Kruger also has
his staple autumnal wear,

00:10:39.410 --> 00:10:43.340
the sweater, the filthy
hat, the Dockers, the glove.

00:10:43.340 --> 00:10:46.220
Sure, it may not be quite
as strong as adamantium

00:10:46.220 --> 00:10:49.010
but Wolverine can only use
his claws when he's awake

00:10:49.010 --> 00:10:51.110
or having a really intense dream.

00:10:51.110 --> 00:10:54.883
Like, what happens constantly
to those teens on Elm Street?

00:10:58.910 --> 00:11:01.690
What separates Fred from the
pack is his speaking ability,

00:11:01.690 --> 00:11:05.280
yeah, he can talk, as a matter
of fact, he won't shut up.

00:11:05.280 --> 00:11:06.640
- Wanna suck face?

00:11:06.640 --> 00:11:08.860
I don't believe in fairytales!

00:11:08.860 --> 00:11:10.490
Bon appetite, bitch.

00:11:10.490 --> 00:11:13.080
- His one liners are part
and parcel for any good entry

00:11:13.080 --> 00:11:15.080
into the "Nightmare on Elm Street" canon.

00:11:15.080 --> 00:11:17.150
Sure, they occasionally get ridiculous

00:11:17.150 --> 00:11:19.050
but it's hard to accuse him of dad jokes

00:11:19.050 --> 00:11:20.810
when you're running for your life.

00:11:20.810 --> 00:11:23.260
Plus, it gives him a
backup career as a comic,

00:11:23.260 --> 00:11:25.993
for tickets, head to unclefreddyslays.net.

00:11:27.145 --> 00:11:27.978
- Got your nose!

00:11:29.369 --> 00:11:30.202
(woman screams)

00:11:30.202 --> 00:11:32.260
References by everyone
from the Fresh Prince

00:11:32.260 --> 00:11:34.500
and DJ Jazzy Jeff to Nicki Minaj

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:36.500
have kept Freddy Kruger alive and well

00:11:36.500 --> 00:11:37.900
in the cultural zeitgeist,

00:11:37.900 --> 00:11:40.110
plus, he had Dokken do his soundtrack

00:11:40.110 --> 00:11:41.220
for the "Dream Warriors,"

00:11:41.220 --> 00:11:44.890
which proves that the music
in hell kicks way more ass.

00:11:44.890 --> 00:11:47.060
So now it looks like only Jason Vorhees

00:11:47.060 --> 00:11:49.372
is standing in the way
of another Freddy round

00:11:49.372 --> 00:11:51.247
- I'll let Jason have some fun.

00:11:53.251 --> 00:11:54.084
- You hear that?

00:11:54.084 --> 00:11:56.030
The dude doesn't even
need a proper theme song,

00:11:56.030 --> 00:11:58.630
he can just chill us by
queuing up that weird breathing

00:11:58.630 --> 00:12:00.190
track on Pro Tools.

00:12:00.190 --> 00:12:02.160
And while Jason certainly
won't be competing

00:12:02.160 --> 00:12:05.160
against Michael Phelps for
swimming records anytime soon,

00:12:05.160 --> 00:12:07.980
his contribution to
athletics is undeniable,

00:12:07.980 --> 00:12:10.710
that hockey mask, it already look to neat

00:12:10.710 --> 00:12:13.140
but now that a serial
killer from beyond the grave

00:12:13.140 --> 00:12:15.220
has donned one, it's the go to mask

00:12:15.220 --> 00:12:18.680
for anyone needing a last
second costume party idea.

00:12:18.680 --> 00:12:20.540
Jason has made the rounds including

00:12:20.540 --> 00:12:23.360
winning an MTV Lifetime Achievement Award

00:12:23.360 --> 00:12:25.140
appearing on the "Arsenio Hall Show"

00:12:25.140 --> 00:12:27.410
and blessing us with
some of our first degrees

00:12:27.410 --> 00:12:28.660
of Kevin Bacon.

00:12:28.660 --> 00:12:30.360
But it's not just the fame of Jason

00:12:30.360 --> 00:12:33.170
or his banned Nike commercial
that makes him an icon,

00:12:33.170 --> 00:12:35.770
it's the day he represents.

00:12:35.770 --> 00:12:38.240
So, the curse of Friday the 13th

00:12:38.240 --> 00:12:41.100
actually finds its
origins well before 1980,

00:12:41.100 --> 00:12:43.560
it dates back to early
Christian mythology.

00:12:43.560 --> 00:12:45.370
Friday was the day of the last supper

00:12:45.370 --> 00:12:48.300
and who is the last apostle
to show up at Applebee's?

00:12:48.300 --> 00:12:51.300
Yep, it was Judas, that Judas.

00:12:51.300 --> 00:12:54.910
He was the 13th guest on that Friday

00:12:54.910 --> 00:12:57.030
but all the Jesus plus ones in the world

00:12:57.030 --> 00:12:59.700
can't compete with what
that day represents now,

00:12:59.700 --> 00:13:01.580
when a Friday the 13th hits,

00:13:01.580 --> 00:13:03.530
weird things happen to people.

00:13:03.530 --> 00:13:05.860
Some folks stay indoors,
call in sick to work,

00:13:05.860 --> 00:13:08.670
shut the blinds, others
celebrate it with a party

00:13:08.670 --> 00:13:11.240
that even the earliest of
All Hallows' Eve participants

00:13:11.240 --> 00:13:13.620
would appreciate and why is all that?

00:13:13.620 --> 00:13:16.030
Because of Jason Vorhees.

00:13:16.030 --> 00:13:18.550
Had it not been for his
consistent pole position

00:13:18.550 --> 00:13:20.310
lodged in the forefront of our brains,

00:13:20.310 --> 00:13:22.130
every time we go camping,

00:13:22.130 --> 00:13:25.670
watch an NHL game and especially
wake up on certain Fridays,

00:13:25.670 --> 00:13:28.400
no one would bat an eye
at the 13th of the month

00:13:28.400 --> 00:13:31.320
but thanks to Jason, with a
hockey assist from his mom,

00:13:31.320 --> 00:13:34.260
Pam, Friday the 13th
and is favorite mascot

00:13:34.260 --> 00:13:37.200
serve as a looming
reminder to tread lightly.

00:13:37.200 --> 00:13:40.010
Jason gets the wind and round
three and once you know it,

00:13:40.010 --> 00:13:41.675
we're all tied up going into,

00:13:41.675 --> 00:13:43.640
let's see if you're a hockey fan,

00:13:43.640 --> 00:13:47.070
we've already had three
periods, so overtime?

00:13:47.070 --> 00:13:48.960
And yes Freddy, this one's for you.

00:13:48.960 --> 00:13:50.270
It's sudden death!

00:13:50.270 --> 00:13:53.410
- Sticks and stone may break my bones

00:13:54.919 --> 00:13:59.070
but nothin' will ever kill me.

00:13:59.070 --> 00:14:03.020
- And now it's time for the
wild card round, iconic moments.

00:14:03.020 --> 00:14:04.770
Okay, because this is a safe space

00:14:04.770 --> 00:14:06.640
where we can be honest with one another,

00:14:06.640 --> 00:14:08.250
this round is all about kills,

00:14:08.250 --> 00:14:09.920
I didn't wanna shout that from the rooftop

00:14:09.920 --> 00:14:11.210
at the beginning of the episode

00:14:11.210 --> 00:14:13.200
but now that you've
stuck with me this long,

00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:15.810
who's the best at fictional murdering?

00:14:15.810 --> 00:14:17.740
Step right up Voorhees family,

00:14:17.740 --> 00:14:19.640
Like any great mother, Mrs. Jason

00:14:19.640 --> 00:14:22.670
did her son a huge solid
by showing him the ropes.

00:14:22.670 --> 00:14:25.080
Unfortunately, these ropes
were actually machetes

00:14:25.080 --> 00:14:27.125
and chain saws, you know what,

00:14:27.125 --> 00:14:28.940
maybe she wasn't that
good of a mom but oh boy,

00:14:28.940 --> 00:14:31.110
was her son ever good at killing!

00:14:31.110 --> 00:14:33.070
Jason punched the dude's head clean off

00:14:33.070 --> 00:14:35.610
when he took Manhattan, he
just popped that sucker out

00:14:35.610 --> 00:14:36.960
like it was tee ball.

00:14:36.960 --> 00:14:38.870
And in "Friday the 13th" part four,

00:14:38.870 --> 00:14:41.850
check out the sick corkscrew
maneuver that Jason performs

00:14:41.850 --> 00:14:45.637
on none other than Mr.
George McFly, Crispin Glover.

00:14:45.637 --> 00:14:48.717
"Hey you, get your damn hands off him."

00:14:53.040 --> 00:14:55.290
But my favorite Jason moment
is when he straight up

00:14:55.290 --> 00:14:57.260
folds a poor sucker in half,

00:14:57.260 --> 00:15:00.130
like he's breaking down
boxes to be a good recycler.

00:15:00.130 --> 00:15:01.410
This kill happens in the film

00:15:01.410 --> 00:15:03.090
where Freddy and Jason square off,

00:15:03.090 --> 00:15:04.740
they weren't just batting over turf,

00:15:04.740 --> 00:15:08.040
it was a war to see who is
the best baddy of all time.

00:15:08.040 --> 00:15:11.730
So now, the undead demon from
Elm Street has the floor.

00:15:11.730 --> 00:15:15.450
- [Freddy] It's time to
put this bad dog to sleep.

00:15:15.450 --> 00:15:18.280
- I love Freddy because so
many of his kills are on brand,

00:15:18.280 --> 00:15:19.830
the guy haunts you in your dreams,

00:15:19.830 --> 00:15:22.520
so naturally he loves a
good bedroom bloodbath.

00:15:22.520 --> 00:15:24.760
Johnny Depp gets sucked into his own bed

00:15:24.760 --> 00:15:28.100
but Fred also got in on the
late eighties waterbed craze

00:15:28.100 --> 00:15:29.670
as evidenced in the "Dream Master."

00:15:29.670 --> 00:15:31.457
- How's this for a wet dream?

00:15:31.457 --> 00:15:32.830
- For the best Kruger kills,

00:15:32.830 --> 00:15:36.000
go down to "Nightmare on Elm
Street 3: Dream Warriors."

00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:38.790
A group of troubled teens,
many struggling with addiction,

00:15:38.790 --> 00:15:42.180
now have to wrestle with
burns bastard son too?

00:15:42.180 --> 00:15:43.780
And it didn't go well,

00:15:43.780 --> 00:15:46.290
poor Tina finally gets to be on television

00:15:46.290 --> 00:15:47.730
but not in the way she hoped

00:15:47.730 --> 00:15:49.600
and this fella became
a literal meat puppet

00:15:49.600 --> 00:15:52.937
years before that band hit it
big with "Backwater Swirl."

00:15:54.520 --> 00:15:56.210
But more so than any one kill,

00:15:56.210 --> 00:15:59.380
it's the spirit of the sick
demented fun that Freddy brings

00:15:59.380 --> 00:16:02.514
to each tragedy that keeps
us coming back for more.

00:16:02.514 --> 00:16:03.931
- Let's get high.

00:16:08.043 --> 00:16:10.260
As opposed to say, Michael Myers,

00:16:10.260 --> 00:16:11.970
who rather than sick pleasure,

00:16:11.970 --> 00:16:14.450
seems to be motivated
by a constantly running

00:16:14.450 --> 00:16:18.020
set of batteries hell
bent on Halloween mayhem.

00:16:18.020 --> 00:16:20.410
From poor Bob in the first "Halloween,"

00:16:20.410 --> 00:16:22.370
Can we check how many fella's named Bob

00:16:22.370 --> 00:16:24.440
actually survive horror movies?

00:16:24.440 --> 00:16:25.700
I'm betting not a lot,

00:16:25.700 --> 00:16:27.770
maybe go by Robert from now on.

00:16:27.770 --> 00:16:30.610
And then as if being named
Karen wasn't already tough,

00:16:30.610 --> 00:16:33.730
look at what happens to
this one in "Halloween II"

00:16:33.730 --> 00:16:36.150
Rob Zombie's "Halloween"
film saw the gruesome end

00:16:36.150 --> 00:16:38.820
of our beloved Octavia Spencer's character

00:16:38.820 --> 00:16:41.820
as well as the seemingly
indestructible Machete himself,

00:16:41.820 --> 00:16:43.230
Danny Trejo.

00:16:43.230 --> 00:16:44.630
Doesn't matter who you are,

00:16:44.630 --> 00:16:48.060
Michael Myers is there to kill
you a quick and permanent.

00:16:48.060 --> 00:16:49.410
And while both he and Jason

00:16:49.410 --> 00:16:51.870
may not be the most
personable of movie villains,

00:16:51.870 --> 00:16:54.280
they got their job done
with ruthless efficiency

00:16:54.280 --> 00:16:55.980
and permanently altered our perception

00:16:55.980 --> 00:16:58.715
of Halloween and Friday the 13th.

00:16:58.715 --> 00:16:59.592
- Help me!

00:16:59.592 --> 00:17:00.652
Help me!

00:17:00.652 --> 00:17:02.819
Somebody, please, help me!

00:17:06.340 --> 00:17:07.500
- [Mark] But it's Freddy Kruger

00:17:07.500 --> 00:17:10.000
who not only used his
glove, his imagination

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:13.010
and his ability to infiltrate
dreams to win our hearts,

00:17:13.010 --> 00:17:14.040
It was his mouth.

00:17:14.040 --> 00:17:15.810
- Ever play in the cat?

00:17:16.953 --> 00:17:18.100
- [Mark] Perhaps he spent
a little too much time

00:17:18.100 --> 00:17:20.140
on the wise cracks in a few of the films

00:17:20.140 --> 00:17:22.150
but he's the consummate entertainer,

00:17:22.150 --> 00:17:24.910
he knows he's there to kill
teens as a means of revenge

00:17:24.910 --> 00:17:27.060
for their parents burning
him alive years ago.

00:17:27.060 --> 00:17:28.490
But Freddy is also well aware

00:17:28.490 --> 00:17:31.520
there's an audience of millions
witnessing the carnage.

00:17:31.520 --> 00:17:33.920
As much as he doesn't care
about the lives of victims,

00:17:33.920 --> 00:17:37.640
he does care about giving us
the most bang for our buck,

00:17:37.640 --> 00:17:40.270
the jokes, the creativity, the passion.

00:17:40.270 --> 00:17:42.110
Whether he's in some random bedroom

00:17:42.110 --> 00:17:44.770
or on his home court,
basement boiler room,

00:17:44.770 --> 00:17:46.900
Freddy Kruger is the horror movie villain

00:17:46.900 --> 00:17:50.410
that gives us his all every
time he foot in our dreams.

00:17:50.410 --> 00:17:53.920
For that, he wins this
round and thus the match.

00:17:53.920 --> 00:17:56.180
- I beat my high score.

00:17:56.180 --> 00:17:59.450
- Freddy, Michael, Jason,
you're all winners in my book.

00:17:59.450 --> 00:18:00.470
And I'm not just saying that

00:18:00.470 --> 00:18:03.110
because I prefer to not
be hacked to pieces,

00:18:03.110 --> 00:18:06.100
you are the champions but
it's been no bed of roses

00:18:06.100 --> 00:18:08.010
for the legions of kills you've committed

00:18:08.010 --> 00:18:11.080
for both personal reasons
and our entertainment value.

00:18:11.080 --> 00:18:13.030
For funsies, you want to
know which of the big three

00:18:13.030 --> 00:18:14.140
has killed the most?

00:18:14.140 --> 00:18:16.600
It's Jason, making his mama proud,

00:18:16.600 --> 00:18:20.250
the big goalie is hovering
it around 157 kills,

00:18:20.250 --> 00:18:23.760
edging out Michael Myers' total of 140.

00:18:23.760 --> 00:18:27.060
Freddy is bringing up the
rear at barely 40 kills

00:18:27.060 --> 00:18:30.460
but today's match was about
quality over quantity.

00:18:30.460 --> 00:18:32.690
Jason might win if all
three were tossed into a pit

00:18:32.690 --> 00:18:35.490
and had to duke it out, all
other things being equal,

00:18:35.490 --> 00:18:37.600
I'd give the tie breaker to a mom,

00:18:37.600 --> 00:18:39.370
but not the mom you think.

00:18:39.370 --> 00:18:42.340
Let's shout out Amanda
Kruger, Freddy's mom,

00:18:42.340 --> 00:18:45.840
she pops up in "Dream Warriors"
as this ominous looking nun

00:18:45.840 --> 00:18:48.420
and I think she's trying
to help Nancy and the gang

00:18:48.420 --> 00:18:51.620
but her mere presence
scares the hell out of me.

00:18:51.620 --> 00:18:54.560
Maybe it's the fact that she
gave birth to a child murderer

00:18:54.560 --> 00:18:55.760
or that she's a ghost

00:18:55.760 --> 00:18:58.060
or that she's wearing
the all white nun look,

00:18:58.060 --> 00:19:01.160
the away uniform for any sister of mercy.

00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:04.000
Man did he give us the best
horror movie villain there is,

00:19:04.000 --> 00:19:05.520
the hat, the sweater,

00:19:05.520 --> 00:19:08.330
the guy who's probably playing
the Jacksonville Comedy Zone

00:19:08.330 --> 00:19:09.200
this weekend.

00:19:09.200 --> 00:19:11.650
Now coming to the stage,
grab your crucifix,

00:19:11.650 --> 00:19:13.640
it's Freddy Krueger.

00:19:13.640 --> 00:19:15.290
But that's just one guy's opinion

00:19:15.290 --> 00:19:16.700
and I don't live on Elm Street,

00:19:16.700 --> 00:19:19.020
I've never been camping and
haven't trick or treated

00:19:19.020 --> 00:19:20.760
in at least 11 months.

00:19:20.760 --> 00:19:22.570
So now it's your turn,

00:19:22.570 --> 00:19:24.570
vote in the comments
section for who you think

00:19:24.570 --> 00:19:26.060
is the best of the bad.

00:19:26.060 --> 00:19:29.100
Freddy, Jason or the O.G, Michael.

00:19:29.100 --> 00:19:30.410
Thanks for watching everyone.

00:19:30.410 --> 00:19:32.950
And remember, don't go
into any wooded areas,

00:19:32.950 --> 00:19:36.010
avoid anyone named Strode on Halloween

00:19:36.010 --> 00:19:38.023
and nap with a buddy?

00:19:39.385 --> 00:19:40.785
Yeah, good luck with the sleep thing.

00:19:40.785 --> 00:19:43.952
(gentle upbeat music)

